claim.claim-text:
a pivot seat unit (10, 10', 10", 100) including at least three pivot pins (15, 15', 15", 150) that are angularly spaced apart from each other about an axial line (L), each of said pivot pins (15, 15', 15", 150) having a central line (L1); and
at least three support units (20, 20", 200, 200') disposed about the axial line (L), each of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') including a support rod (21) that has an extending axis (X), and a push member (22, 220') that is fixedly connected to said support rod (21), said support rod (21) of each of said support units (20, 20", 200) having a first end portion (211), a second end portion (212) that is opposite to said first end portion (211) along the extending axis (X), and a pivot portion (214) that is located between said first end portion (211) and said second end portion (212) and that is pivotally connected to a respective one of said pivot pins (15, 15', 15", 150), said push member (22, 220') of each of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') being located between said pivot portion (214) and said second end portion (212) of said support rod (21) of said support unit (20, 20", 200), and having first and second push surfaces (224a, 224b), said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') being convertible between a folded state and an unfolded state;
wherein, when said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') are in the folded state, said first end portions (211) of said support rods (21) of said support units (20, 20", 200) are proximate to the axial line (L), said second end portions (212) of said support rods (21) of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') are proximate to the axial line (L), and for each of said push members (22, 220') of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200'), said first push surface (224a, 224a') of said push member (22, 220') faces said second push surface (224b, 224b') of an adjacent one of said push members (22, 220'), and said second push surface (224b, 224b') of said push member (22, 220') faces said first push surface (224a, 224a') of the other adjacent one of said push members (22, 220');
wherein, when said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') are in the unfolded state, said first end portions (211) of said support rods (21) of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') are distal from the axial line (L), and said second end portions (212) of said support rods (21) of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') are distal from the axial line (L); and
wherein, rotation of any one of said support rods (21) of said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') relative to said pivot seat unit (10, 10', 10", 100) drives a circumferentially adjacent one of said support rods (21) to rotate, such that when any one of said support rods (21) is rotated relative to said pivot seat unit (10, 10', 10", 100) about the central line (L1) of the respective one of said pivot pins (15, 15', 15", 150), the others of said support rods (21) are in turn driven to rotate relative to said pivot seat unit (10, 10', 10", 100) so as to convert said support units (20, 20", 200, 200') between the folded state and the unfolded state.
